  "instructions": "## Two subnets, one router\n\nThe library PCs are on `192.168.1.0/24` and the office server is on `192.168.2.0/24`. The router R1 sits between them with an interface in each subnet. Every address is already set, but the PCs have **no default gateway**, so they do not know where to send traffic for the other subnet.\n\n## Do this\n\n1. Ping the server from PC1 and read why it fails.\n2. Click each PC and set its **default gateway** to the router interface on its own subnet.\n3. Ping again, then press **Check my network**.",
